         :names
         {:g
          "The sample is the first direct probe of the claimed retrieval property rather than a proxy."},
         :axioms #{}}},
       :I1
       {:text
        "    The acceptance signal checks a representation of the property rather than\n    the property itself, especially when imports, definitions, historical\n    state, or human verdicts contribute to the claim.\n",
        :source
        {:path
         "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg",
         :sha256
         "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"},
        :situation-source
        "Fragment 1165-1211 'weighting and the first hand-labeled sample.'",
        :theory
        {:elems #{:i1},
         :names
         {:i1
          "A hand-labeled sample is proposed as the acceptance signal for weighting."},
         :axioms #{}}},
       :I2
       {:text
        "    Direct probes can be expensive, and some properties have no complete\n    decision procedure.  A dependency-closure audit may require building\n    previously unbuilt artifacts; a semantic vacuity check remains heuristic.\n    Calling an incomplete probe complete merely creates a new proxy.  State the\n    probe's coverage, retain explicit unknown/skipped outcomes, and reserve\n    acceptance for the portion actually checked.\n",
